					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vaelynx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(914331); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=914331&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606164000" alt="VAElynx" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=914331)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vaelynx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(914331); return false;" >VAElynx</a></span> <span class="odate time_1410641050 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Sep 2014 20:44</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2109209">
									

<p>In all honesty, I found the punchline rather trite and I second the inexplicable english comment by Thekillerax (the same thing that bugged me about the &quot;To Serve Man&quot; twilight zone episode - that a double-entendre like that inexplicably worked in an alien language, nvm how the hell did they translate it).</p>
<p>Also, couple minor problems.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2468 tends to appear in populated yet open areas, including urban parks and town squares. The subject has shown a tendency to revisit places which have resulted in a successful yield.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why is it referred to suddenly as subject after being called entity for two paragraphs before? Makes it sound as if you're talking about something else.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Upon reaching a distance of thirty-five centimeters from SCP-2468, victims are lifted by an unknown force to a height of approximately two meters, and dematerialize completely, along with SCP-2468.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence is confusing, straight after describing calls for help, it suddenly talks about victims. I suggest this replacement.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If a living organism of sufficient size ([describe limits, author]) approaches within 35cm of SCP-2468, it is lifted by an unknown force to a height of approximately two metres, then dematerializes, along with SCP-2468.</p>
</blockquote>

